On Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:24:12 -0700, Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com> wrote:
> I have a dedicated mail account. I'm trying to keep things simple right
> now. Just sync the whole thing. Stop making this so complicated.

Understood, and sorry for the churn. The reader restriction is gone.
The ACL is back to "anyone may list and read", and mbsync syncs every
folder.

> Keep things simple. Deliver new mail to INBOX. Sync the maildir. That's
> it.

Done in "[PATCH v7 0/9] jails/instances/lab-mail: Build the list's
mail hub" [1]:

- The Sieve patch is dropped. LMTP delivers each post to INBOX.
- INBOX is part of the maildir, so mbsync syncs it like any other
  folder. A post reaches Fastmail and every reader on the next sync.
- The lists folder is dropped too. The spec no longer has a Fastmail
  rule filing into it, and the jj maildir import goes into INBOX.
  Mail to the list addresses lands in INBOX on Fastmail as well, so
  you can remove that rule once this is on the jail.
- There are no manual steps. You no longer need to move anything out
  of the old INBOX.

The interdiff against v6 is in the cover letter. Dovecot isn't
installed here, so the configs were not run on a jail.

